The analysis engine
-------------------
lexcode runs Opengrep (https://github.com/opengrep/opengrep) as a separate
program. Opengrep is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 (LGPL-2.1). lexcode does not include, link or modify Opengrep: on
first use it downloads the unmodified release binary pinned in
src/engine/pin.ts from the Opengrep GitHub release and checks its sha256.

The exact source of the pinned release is available at
https://github.com/opengrep/opengrep/tree/v1.33.1 and
https://github.com/opengrep/opengrep/archive/refs/tags/v1.33.1.tar.gz

The full text of the LGPL-2.1 is at
https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html

If UnGovr ever patches Opengrep, the patched source is published under the
LGPL-2.1.

